  "result": "Fixed! The issue was in `src/lib/mentions.ts`:\n\n**Root cause**: The `extractMentions()` function had access to a `withoutCode()` helper that removes code blocks, but it was never using it. This meant mentions inside fenced code blocks were incorrectly extracted and triggered notifications.\n\n**Changes made**:\n1. **`extractMentions()`** - Now calls `withoutCode(body)` before extracting mentions, so mentions inside code blocks are ignored before being passed to the notification system.\n2. **`highlightMentions()`** - Also fixed to check if each mention is inside a code block (by building a list of code block ranges) before wrapping it with highlight styling, ensuring consistent behavior with extraction.\n\nThe fixes ensure that text inside fenced code blocks (```...```) and inline code (backticks) is properly excluded from notification mentions.",
